 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and authorization
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request. Keys are configured in
+`apiKeys` in the data file. Viewers can use GET routes except `/audit`; cooks
+can also cook recipes, record waste, log temperatures and enter stock-take
+counts. Managers can use every route. Missing or unknown keys return 401
+(`unauthorized`); insufficient permissions return 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+Successful data-changing requests are recorded with their time, key name,
+method, path and response status. `GET /audit` returns entries newest first
+and is restricted to managers.
+
+## Routes
+
+See the complete route list under Routes in `README.md`, including `GET /audit`.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
